silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_02_probe_tsn_identity_concrete_anchor_3 silm:hasExample "In 'ProbeTsnIdentityAnchorBareTsnNumeric', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, The bare numeric value 183798 considered apart from its containing ITIS row. In the R2 probe diagram, this is the dashed-red source node attempting a direct identity arrow to Mittens. It has no typed legs in O_01: no record leg, no measurement leg, no role leg; only a string/integer literal. The forbidden dashed arrow demonstrates that an identifier-as-field cannot replace an apex that requires a full ten-leg cocone.." .
